      "hints": [
        "Differentiate using the chain rule, multiplying by $3$ for each term.",
        "Examine the sign of $f'(x)$ for $x > 2$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Differentiate $f(x) = 4(3x - 6)^{-2} + (3x - 6)^{-3}$ with respect to $x$ using the chain rule:\n$$f'(x) = 4(-2)(3x - 6)^{-3}(3) + (-3)(3x - 6)^{-4}(3) = -24(3x - 6)^{-3} - 9(3x - 6)^{-4}$$",
        "Rewrite as algebraic fractions:\n$$f'(x) = -\\frac{24}{(3x - 6)^3} - \\frac{9}{(3x - 6)^4}$$",
        "Evaluate the sign of $f'(x)$ for the domain $x > 2$:\n$$x > 2 \\implies 3x - 6 > 0 \\implies (3x - 6)^3 > 0 \\text{ and } (3x - 6)^4 > 0$$\n$$f'(x) = -\\left[\\frac{24}{(3x - 6)^3} + \\frac{9}{(3x - 6)^4}\\right] < 0$$",
        "Conclude that $f$ is a decreasing function for all $x > 2$."
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
          "Derivative & Decreasing Function": "Differentiates to $-24(3x-6)^{-3} - 9(3x-6)^{-4}$ (B3), and justifies that $f'(x) < 0$ for $x > 2$ so $f$ is decreasing (B1)."
        },
        "criteria_source": "mark_scheme_structured"
      }
